  "id": "trait-theory",
  "term": "trait theory",
  "definition": "Trait theory is the view that personality can be understood in terms of relatively stable traits, which are consistent patterns in how a person thinks, feels, and behaves. In this context, traits are used to explain enduring individual differences, including vulnerability to psychological difficulties.",
